Article 9 The types of administrative compulsory measures include:
(1) Restriction of personal freedom of citizens;
(2) Seizure of premises, facilities, or property;
(3) Impoundment of property;
(4) Freezing of deposits or remittances;
(5) Other administrative compulsory measures.

Article 12 The methods of administrative compulsory enforcement include:
(1) Imposition of an additional fine or late fee;
(2) Transfer of deposits or remittances;
(3) Auction or lawful disposal of seized or impounded premises, facilities, or property;
(4) Removal of obstacles and restoration to the original condition;
(5) Substituted performance;
(6) Other methods of compulsory enforcement.

Article 55 To apply to a People's Court for compulsory enforcement, an administrative organ shall provide the following materials:
(1) A written application for compulsory enforcement;
(2) The written administrative decision, along with the facts, reasons, and basis thereof;
(3) The opinions of the party and the status of the administrative organ's urging;
(4) Information on the subject matter of the requested compulsory enforcement;
(5) Other materials as prescribed by laws and administrative regulations.
The written application for compulsory enforcement shall be signed by the responsible person of the administrative organ, affixed with the seal of the administrative organ, and dated.

Article 61 Where an administrative organ, in implementing administrative compulsion, commits any of the following acts, the administrative organ at the next higher level or the relevant department shall order it to make corrections, and the persons directly in charge and the other persons directly responsible shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) the act has no basis in laws or regulations;
(2) the subject, conditions or manner of administrative compulsion is altered;
(3) the administrative compulsion is implemented in violation of statutory procedures;
(4) administrative compulsory enforcement is implemented at night or on statutory holidays in violation of the provisions of this Law;
(5) the residents are forced to perform relevant administrative decisions by means of cutting off water, electricity, gas supply, heat supply, etc.; or
(6) other circumstances in which the administrative compulsion is illegally implemented.

Article 62 Where an administrative organ, in violation of the provisions of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the administrative organ at the next higher level or the relevant department shall order it to make corrections, and the persons directly in charge and the other persons directly responsible shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) the scope of sealing up, seizure or freezing is expanded;
(2) the sealed-up or seized premises, facilities or property are used or damaged;
(3) no decision on disposition is made within the statutory period for sealing up or seizure, or the sealing up or seizure is not released in a timely manner according to law; or
(4) no decision on disposition is made within the statutory period for freezing deposits or remittances, or the freezing is not released in a timely manner according to law.

Article 65 Where a financial institution, in violation of the provisions of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the financial regulatory authority shall order it to make corrections, and the persons directly in charge and the other persons directly responsible shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) disclosing information to a party before freezing;
(2) failing to freeze or transfer the deposits or remittances that should be frozen or transferred immediately, thereby causing the deposits or remittances to be transferred;
(3) freezing or transferring the deposits or remittances that should not be frozen or transferred; or
(4) failing to release the freeze on deposits or remittances in a timely manner.
